# Migrations are checksummed by tools/db/migrate.ts, and the checksum is taken
# over the file's bytes. With core.autocrlf=true Git rewrites these to CRLF on
# checkout while `schema_migration` holds the LF checksums recorded when they
# were applied — so every migration reads as "edited since it was applied", and
# `db:migrate` refuses to run at the first one. Pinning them to LF makes the
# working copy match what Git stores and what the database recorded.
oxvercity/db/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
